            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> what are we supposed to do if the LS gives us a path like /people_.$personId.tsx ?\n\nHere are the relevant lines from the gist linked above (on NVIM v0.13.0-dev-1315+g69e61d52e2, so before #41398 was merged):\n\n```\n[DEBUG][2026-08-14 17:15:44] /usr/local/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/client.lua:764\t\"LSP[bugged-ls]\"\t\"client.request\"\t1\t\"textDocument/definition\"\t{ position = { character = 31, line = 0 }, textDocument = { uri = \"file:///home/matt/dev/nvim_lsp_dollar_sign_bug/a.$b.tsx\" } }\t<function 1>\t1\n[DEBUG][2026-08-14 17:15:44] /usr/local/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/rpc.lua:353\t\"rpc.send\"\t{ id = 6, jsonrpc = \"2.0\", method = \"textDocument/definition\", params = { position = { character = 31, line = 0 }, textDocument = { uri = \"file:///home/matt/dev/nvim_lsp_dollar_sign_bug/a.$b.tsx\" } } }\n[DEBUG][2026-08-14 17:15:44] /usr/local/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/rpc.lua:444\t\"rpc.receive\"\t{ id = 6, jsonrpc = \"2.0\", result = { { originSelectionRange = { [\"end\"] = { character = 32, line = 0 }, start = { character = 31, line = 0 } }, targetRange = { [\"end\"] = { character = 20, line = 0 }, start = { character = 11, line = 0 } }, targetSelectionRange = { [\"end\"] = { character = 12, line = 0 }, start = { character = 11, line = 0 } }, targetUri = \"file:///home/matt/dev/nvim_lsp_dollar_sign_bug/a.%24b.tsx\" } } }\n[DEBUG][2026-08-14 17:15:44] /usr/local/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/rpc.lua:444\t\"rpc.receive\"\t{ jsonrpc = \"2.0\", method = \"window/logMessage\", params = { message = \"handled method 'textDocument/definition' (6) in 1.136388ms\", type = 3 } }\n[INFO][2026-08-14 17:15:44] /usr/local/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/handlers.lua:609\t\"handled method 'textDocument/definition' (6) in 1.136388ms\"\n```\n\nThe language server returns `targetUri = \"file:///home/matt/dev/nvim_lsp_dollar_sign_bug/a.%24b.tsx\"`. I would expect nvim to url decode it to `/home/matt/dev/nvim_lsp_dollar_sign_bug/a.$b.tsx` and treat that as a literal string for the path of the file to navigate to. Instead, when running the code from the PR, it seems to escape the dollar sign with a backslash, then try to open the _literal_ path `/home/matt/dev/nvim_lsp_dollar_sign_bug/a.\\$b.tsx` (which I have verified by creating a file at that literal path and observing Neovim navigate into it).\n\n> need to see the stacktrace of that error.\n\nI'd be happy to provide it, if I can work out how.\n\nThere is no stacktrace provided alongside the message. The contents of lsp.log look similar to the above when I run on NVIM v0.13.0-dev-1404+g92d5531f96. There's nothing relevant in nvim.log, even if I first run `:lua vim.log:set_level(vim.log.levels.TRACE)`.\n\nThe whole message that nvim gives me is `E429: File \"/home/matt/dev/nvim_lsp_dollar_sign_bug/a.\\$b.tsx\" does not exist` (there are no more lines).\n",
