        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "In case it saves anyone else some time: I noticed that, in bash, the filename renders as 'a.$b.tsx', so I wondered if wrapping the filename in single quotes would work to get the path string treated as a literal.\n\n```\n~/dev/nvim_lsp_dollar_sign_bug\n❯ ll\n...\n-rw-rw-r--  1 matt matt    35 Aug 26 12:39 'a.$b.tsx'\n...\n```\n\nI tried an appropriate modification to neovim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/_tagfunc.lua, but it didn't work either: `E429: File \"/home/matt/dev/nvim_lsp_dollar_sign_bug/'a.$b.tsx'\" does not exist`\n",
